# Logging & observability

Practice aligns with python-services `logging-loguru.mdc` and ios
`logging-observability.mdc`: structured fields, not string soup.

## Hard rules

1. Prefer discrete fields (device_id, correlation_id, error_kind) over
   interpolating identifiers only into free text.
2. **Never** log secrets (keys, PEMs, tokens, join material).
3. Choose a single logging facade for the daemon; do not mix ad-hoc `println!`
   for production paths.

Sink/backend (journald, file, OTel) is consumer ADR / foundation default.

